  "slug": "furnal-equinox",
  "name": "Furnal Equinox",
  "shortName": "FE",
  "description": "Furnal Equinox is an annual furry convention in Toronto, Ontario, run as a non-profit event by Anthropomorphic Events of Ontario. Its name refers to the spring equinox, as the convention was traditionally held in March. The first edition, in March 2010 at the DoubleTree by Hilton Toronto Airport, drew 330 attendees. The convention later used the Sheraton Toronto Airport Hotel and, from 2017 to 2026, the Westin Harbour Castle, where attendance reached 3,690 in 2025. It raises money for Ontario animal charities, with C$33,746.51 for Procyon Wildlife in 2026. From 2027 it moves to the Sheraton Centre Toronto and to February dates.",
